      {
        "id": 214413,
        "name": "degausser",
        "username": "degausser",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/9fc29f/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-02-28T06:56:32.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So, I had some more things that I wanted to consider.&nbsp; I was thinking about ways to get the PCs into space, just for a brief space adventure (after all, what are comics without a space adventure?) and I was looking for an 'in.'</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>One idea I had was that Wagermaster shows up.&nbsp; He is pretty bored with Heritage now that he is 'boring' and 'mentoring' so he has decided to try being a pain in the neck to other hero teams.&nbsp; He shows up to the PCs, making a big deal of how they are 'lesser' heroes, and offers a wager.&nbsp; He'll give them the oppertunity to save a 'great hero of earth in need of help,' but they have to get him, and themselves, back inside their superhero headquarters within one month, or he'll strand them back where they started with no way to get home.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The hero in question is the de-powered captain cosmic, on that alien refugee planet that he gets stranded on at the end of OblivAeon, and there are all sorts of shenanigans in the story arc of getting home (including Wager Master hiring Greazer to hunt them down, just as a fun wrinkle, reminants of the Thanagarian Empire they encounter, etc.)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I dunno, too goofy?&nbsp; Too much for a more street-level group?&nbsp; Thoughts?</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:45:36.463Z",
